<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
    <head>
        <title>Html Layout Tags</title>
    </head>
    <body>
        <header>
            <h1>HTML Layouts</h1>
        </header>
        <section>
            <nav>
                <ul>
                    <li><a>Content Page 1</a></li>
                    <li><a>Content Page 2</a></li>
                    <li><a>Content Page 3</a></li>
                </ul>
            </nav>
            <article>
                <div>
                <h2>Article</h2>
                    <p>Defines an independent, self-contained content.</p>
                    <p>This is where a piece of content for this page will be displayed. Its likely a bunch of text like this in paragraph form.</p>
                    <p>You will put specific information regarding whatever topic the page is about here. So if it's a recipe page, you might have a list of ingrediants, and step by step instructions on how to apply those ingredients.</p>
                </div>
                <aside>
                    <p>This element defines some content aside from the content it is placed in (like a sidebar).</p>
                    <p>The content in this element should be indirectly related to the surrounding content.</p>
                </aside>
            </article>
        </section>
        <footer>
            <h6>Footer</h6>
            <details>
                <summary>Click to see more</summary>
                <p>This is some hidden content that will appear when the details are expanded.</p>
            </details>
        </footer>
    </body>
</html>